# Secret group `migrate`: The superuser connection that runs migrations. No running service holds it.
# Loaded by: no systemd unit; only deploy.sh, through the transient migration and seed units.
#
# Ownership and mode are load-bearing: `root:root 0600`. systemd reads EnvironmentFile= as root
# before dropping privileges. provision.sh installs this template to
# /opt/semprec/shared/env/migrate.env only when that file does not exist, so an operator's values are
# never overwritten by a rerun, and it never prints a value. A key belongs to exactly one group
# (docs/adr/2026-10-03-per-service-secret-groups.md); this file is excluded from restic backups.

# SEMPREC_MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL: used only by `deploy.sh` (issue #190) to run the migrations CLI,
# which creates roles and grants and so authenticates as POSTGRES_USER in postgres.env — never by a
# long-running service. `deploy.sh` never reads this file itself: systemd loads it into the
# one-off migration and seed units. Built from POSTGRES_USER/POSTGRES_PASSWORD/POSTGRES_DB, e.g.:
# postgres://<POSTGRES_USER>:<POSTGRES_PASSWORD>@127.0.0.1:5432/semprec
SEMPREC_MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL=
